UID:cd2fe76fe3cb3258@role-estate-probate.maine-government-feeds
DTSTAMP:20261002T221147Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261002
SUMMARY:[Curated Role Feeds] To Providers of Adult or Children's Services 
 to Individuals with Intellectual Disabilities (ID) or Autism
DESCRIPTION:Maine.gov\nAgencies\n|\nOnline Services\n|\nHelp\n|\nSearch Ma
 ine.gov\nDHHS\n→\nOffice of MaineCare Services (OMS)\n→\nProvider Reso
 urces\n→\n	 \n			To Providers of Adult or Children's Services to Individ
 uals with Intellectual Disabilities (ID) or Autism\nTo Providers of Adult 
 or Children's Services to Individuals with Intellectual Disabilities (ID) 
 or Autism\nOct 02\, 2026\nThe State of Maine Department of Health and Huma
 n Services (DHHS) Office of Aging and Disability Services (OADS) is planni
 ng to launch the new Lifespan Waiver in May 2027.\nOur first priority is t
 o offer support for future providers of Lifespan services.  Following ou
 r Lifespan Provider Readiness project in 2025\, we are reaching out to und
 erstand provider interest in offering services under Lifespan. To that end
 \, we created a survey to gauge interest from providers who serve individu
 als\nfourteen or older\nwho have ID or autism.\nPlease take a few minutes 
 to\ncomplete this survey\n.\nThe survey will be open until\nFriday\, Octob
 er 16\, at 4:00 PM\n.\nFilling out the survey does not obligate an agency 
 to provide services. We are both gauging interest in particular services\,
  but also gathering contact information so we can provide technical assist
 ance to agencies. For example\, we hope to sustain Communities of Practice
 \, and provide training opportunities.\nFor questions\, please contact the
 \nOADS Lifespan Project\n.\nThank you for your interest\, and we look forw
 ard to being in contact regarding Lifespan.\n~ The OADS Team\nNot yet subs
 cribed to OADS’ email communications?\nClick to subscribe\n.\nhttps://ww
 w.maine.gov/dhhs/oms/providers/provider-bulletins/providers-adult-or-child
 rens-services-individuals-intellectual-disabilities-id-or-autism
URL:https://www.maine.gov/dhhs/oms/providers/provider-bulletins/providers-
 adult-or-childrens-services-individuals-intellectual-disabilities-id-or-au
 tism
CATEGORIES:Curated Role Feeds
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:631761be3bbdf324@role-estate-probate.maine-government-feeds
DTSTAMP:20261002T221118Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261002
SUMMARY:[Curated Role Feeds] Domestic Violence Awareness Month
DESCRIPTION:Hello\, this is Governor Janet Mills\, and thank you for liste
 ning.\nSome years ago\, there was a young woman who dated a man who was ha
 ndsome and charming and smart\, and she was in love with him. That man was
  also an alcoholic\, as it turned out. And one night\, in a drunken rage\,
  he held a gun to her head.\nThe gun did not go off. She packed her bags a
 nd left that place and never turned back. Well\, the rest of the story is 
 that that young woman went to law school. She became a prosecutor\, later 
 Attorney General\, and now the Governor of the State of Maine.\nYes\, I wa
 s one of the lucky ones.\nMany others who experienced domestic abuse are n
 ot so lucky. So to make sure that Maine people who have experienced or who
  are experiencing domestic abuse know that they're not alone and know that
  escape from violence is possible\, I have declared\nOctober Domestic Viol
 ence Awareness Month\nin Maine.\nHere are some things you ought to know ab
 out domestic abuse and domestic violence. Domestic abuse and domestic viol
 ence affect people and families of all races\, ages\, genders\, and income
  levels. Nationwide\, one in four women and one in seven men has experienc
 ed abuse and violence by an intimate partner in their lifetime. In Maine\,
  nearly half of all homicides are related to domestic abuse every year.\nW
 e can prevent domestic abuse and domestic violence in Maine by spreading a
 wareness\, by improving public policies to better support people affected 
 by abuse\, and by holding perpetrators accountable.\nEvery day\, but espec
 ially during Domestic Violence Awareness Month\, may we all do our part to
  spread awareness about domestic abuse\, to challenge the behavior of abus
 ive people\, and to support survivors of abuse\, whoever they may be. Toge
 ther\, our individual actions are what will end domestic abuse in the stat
 e of Maine.\nSo if you or someone you know is experiencing abuse\, please 
 call the statewide Domestic Abuse Helpline at 1-866-834-HELP. That's 1-866
 -834-HELP. If you or someone you know is deaf or h\nhttp://www.maine.gov/g
 overnor/mills/news/radio_address/domestic-violence-awareness-month-2026-10
 -02
URL:http://www.maine.gov/governor/mills/news/radio_address/domestic-violen
 ce-awareness-month-2026-10-02
CATEGORIES:Curated Role Feeds
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
