UID:5a55f34031a88355@role-estate-probate.maine-government-feeds
DTSTAMP:20260930T221247Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260930
SUMMARY:[Curated Role Feeds] Disability Employment Awareness Month - Octob
 er
DESCRIPTION:WHEREAS\n\, October 2026 marks the 81st anniversary of Nationa
 l Disability Employment Awareness Month\; and\nWHEREAS\n\, workplaces acro
 ss our state that are welcoming of the talents of all people\, including p
 eople with disabilities\, are critical to healthy communities and a strong
  economy\; and\nWHEREAS\n\, while the employment rate of people with disab
 ilities ages 16 to 64 in Maine has increased to 44 percent\, it remains si
 gnificantly lower than the 83 percent employment rate for Maine people wit
 hout disabilities\; and\nWHEREAS\n\, it is important that the State of Mai
 ne prepare all youth\, including those with disabilities\, for meaningful 
 careers and an adulthood that includes employment\; and\nWHEREAS\n\, Maine
  is an Employment First state\, affirming employment as the first and pref
 erred option for people with disabilities who receive services from state 
 agencies\; and\nWHEREAS\n\, people with disabilities\, including people wh
 o are Deaf\, Hard of Hearing\, Late Deafened\, Blind or with Low Vision ma
 ke significant contributions to Maine's economy and communities\; and\nWHE
 REAS\n\, activities during this month will reinforce the value and talent 
 people with disabilities add to our workplaces and communities and affirm 
 Maine's commitment to increasing access to good jobs and competitive\, int
 egrated employment for all workers\, including those with disabilities\;\n
 NOW\, THEREFORE\n\, be it resolved that I\, Janet T. Mills\, Governor of t
 he State of Maine\, do hereby proclaim October 2026 as\nDisability Employm
 ent Awareness Month\nthroughout the State of Maine\, and I call upon emplo
 yers\, schools\, higher education institutions and other community organiz
 ations in Maine to observe October with appropriate programs and activitie
 s that celebrate the contributions of people with disabilities and promote
  access to good\, in-demand jobs and career pathways such as registered ap
 prenticeships for all Maine people.\nIn testimony whereof\, I have caused\
 nthe Great Seal of the State to be\nhereunto affixed GIVEN under my\nha\nh
 ttp://www.maine.gov/governor/mills/official_documents/proclamations/2026-0
 9-disability-employment-awareness-month-october
URL:http://www.maine.gov/governor/mills/official_documents/proclamations/2
 026-09-disability-employment-awareness-month-october
CATEGORIES:Curated Role Feeds
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
